  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "6656210",
      "title": "Injecting the Logging Service into Components",
      "lectureOrder": 431,
      "videoOrder": 396,
      "sourceHash": "c9ede4fe1290cf1f68ae138dcf6073fbe9401e70a8dc8c470afa19d96a7f70e0",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.49,
          "end": 4.68,
          "en": "-: In the last lecture, we created our service",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.68,
          "end": 8.04,
          "en": "and I told you to not instantiate it on your own.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.04,
          "end": 10.92,
          "en": "I told you that Angular offers some great tool",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.92,
          "end": 13.8,
          "en": "which will give us access to our services.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.8,
          "end": 17.19,
          "en": "It's Angular's dependency injector.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.19,
          "end": 19.08,
          "en": "What is a dependency injector?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.08,
          "end": 21.84,
          "en": "Well, a dependency is something a class of ours",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.84,
          "end": 22.8,
          "en": "will depend on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 22.8,
          "end": 25.17,
          "en": "For example, the new account component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 25.17,
          "end": 27.06,
          "en": "depends on that logging service",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 27.06,
          "end": 30.36,
          "en": "because we want to call a method in that service.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 30.36,
          "end": 32.88,
          "en": "And the dependence injector",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 32.88,
          "end": 34.95,
          "en": "simply injects this dependency,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 34.95,
          "end": 37.86,
          "en": "injects an instance off this class",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 37.86,
          "end": 40.47,
          "en": "into our component automatically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 40.47,
          "end": 43.53,
          "en": "All we need to do is, we need to inform Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 43.53,
          "end": 46.17,
          "en": "that we require such a instance.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 46.17,
          "end": 50.67,
          "en": "So how do we inform Angular that we require such a instance?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 50.67,
          "end": 53.19,
          "en": "We add a constructor to the class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 53.19,
          "end": 55.2,
          "en": "to the component in this case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 55.2,
          "end": 57.66,
          "en": "where we want to use our service.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 57.66,
          "end": 59.94,
          "en": "So there I can bind it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 59.94,
          "end": 62.37,
          "en": "to a property by using this TypeScript shortcut",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 62.37,
          "end": 65.46,
          "en": "of adding an accessor in front of the name of the argument",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 65.46,
          "end": 68.37,
          "en": "to instantly create a property with the same name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 68.37,
          "end": 70.14,
          "en": "and bind the value to it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 70.14,
          "end": 72.78,
          "en": "So here I will name this logging service.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 72.78,
          "end": 74.78999999999999,
          "en": "This name is totally up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 74.78999999999999,
          "end": 77.03999999999999,
          "en": "Now this is the important part here though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 77.03999999999999,
          "end": 79.26,
          "en": "Add a type assignment here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 79.26,
          "end": 80.55,
          "en": "This is not optional.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 80.55,
          "end": 81.9,
          "en": "You need to set a type,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 81.9,
          "end": 86.1,
          "en": "and the type has to be the class you want to get injected.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 86.1,
          "end": 87.96000000000001,
          "en": "Logging service in this case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 87.96000000000001,
          "end": 91.77,
          "en": "Make sure to also add the import at the top.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 91.77,
          "end": 94.14,
          "en": "Now let me close the body of this constructor.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 94.14,
          "end": 97.41,
          "en": "And this simple task here informs Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 97.41,
          "end": 101.00999999999999,
          "en": "that we will need an instance of this logging service.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 101.00999999999999,
          "end": 104.31,
          "en": "Correctly you might ask, well, how do we inform Angular?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 104.31,
          "end": 107.643,
          "en": "Or why does this matter if we write this in the constructor?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 108.47999999999999,
          "end": 110.75999999999999,
          "en": "Think about who gives us",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 110.75999999999999,
          "end": 113.07,
          "en": "the instance of this account component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 113.07,
          "end": 114.99000000000001,
          "en": "this new account component here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 114.99000000000001,
          "end": 116.58,
          "en": "This is a types of class in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 116.58,
          "end": 119.46000000000001,
          "en": "So somewhere this needs to get instantiated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 119.46000000000001,
          "end": 121.86,
          "en": "so that something happens in our app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 121.86,
          "end": 124.743,
          "en": "Well, who's responsible for creating our components?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 125.61,
          "end": 126.96,
          "en": "Angular is, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 126.96,
          "end": 130.86,
          "en": "because we are placing selectors in our templates.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 130.86,
          "end": 133.11,
          "en": "And when Angular comes across these selectors",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 133.11,
          "end": 136.5,
          "en": "it gives us instances of our components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 136.5,
          "end": 138.36,
          "en": "Now, since Angular is responsible",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 138.36,
          "end": 141.24,
          "en": "for instantiating our components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 141.24,
          "end": 145.59,
          "en": "Angular will need to construct them correctly.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 145.59,
          "end": 147.96,
          "en": "So if we define in the constructor",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 147.96,
          "end": 149.97,
          "en": "that we require some argument,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 149.97,
          "end": 151.95,
          "en": "Angular will recognize this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 151.95,
          "end": 154.8,
          "en": "And now it tries to give us that argument.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 154.8,
          "end": 158.52,
          "en": "It tries to give us this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 158.52,
          "end": 160.07999999999998,
          "en": "well type in this case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 160.07999999999998,
          "end": 164.57999999999998,
          "en": "So it knows we want an instance of the logging service class",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 164.57999999999998,
          "end": 165.603,
          "en": "because we define the type here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 165.603,
          "end": 167.97,
          "en": "This is why this is important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 167.97,
          "end": 170.94,
          "en": "Now that is almost enough, but not quite.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 170.94,
          "end": 173.76,
          "en": "Now Angular knows what we want,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 173.76,
          "end": 177,
          "en": "but it doesn't know how to give us such an instance.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 177,
          "end": 180.24,
          "en": "We need to do one additional step.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 180.24,
          "end": 182.58,
          "en": "We need to provide a service.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 182.58,
          "end": 187.44,
          "en": "Provide simply means we tell Angular how to create it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 187.44,
          "end": 191.19,
          "en": "And that sounds very complicated and it is very simple.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 191.19,
          "end": 193.95,
          "en": "All we have to do is add one extra property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 193.95,
          "end": 196.23,
          "en": "to the at component decorator.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 196.23,
          "end": 199.56,
          "en": "The provider's property here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 199.56,
          "end": 200.94,
          "en": "This also takes an array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 200.94,
          "end": 203.88,
          "en": "like other properties we added before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 203.88,
          "end": 207.99,
          "en": "And here we again just have to specify the type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 207.99,
          "end": 210.84,
          "en": "of what we want to be able to get provided,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 210.84,
          "end": 211.77,
          "en": "you could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 211.77,
          "end": 213.78,
          "en": "So logging service again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 213.78,
          "end": 217.5,
          "en": "Now with that, Angular, when analyzing the component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 217.5,
          "end": 219.96,
          "en": "recognizes that it should be able",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 219.96,
          "end": 221.85,
          "en": "to give us such a logging service",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 221.85,
          "end": 225,
          "en": "and it will set itself up to be able to do so.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 225,
          "end": 227.55,
          "en": "And when it then actually builds the component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 227.55,
          "end": 229.05,
          "en": "constructs it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 229.05,
          "end": 231.78,
          "en": "it sees that we want to have such an instance",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 231.78,
          "end": 234.32999999999998,
          "en": "and it will know how to give us such an instance.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 234.32999999999998,
          "end": 238.02,
          "en": "And now we can simply, in our component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 238.02,
          "end": 239.97,
          "en": "anywhere in this component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 239.97,
          "end": 242.61,
          "en": "access our logging service property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 242.61,
          "end": 244.05,
          "en": "which is created automatically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 244.05,
          "end": 246.6,
          "en": "since I used this type script shortcut here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 246.6,
          "end": 249.36,
          "en": "and call log Status change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 249.36,
          "end": 252.9,
          "en": "So now I'm not creating that instance manually,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 252.9,
          "end": 254.91,
          "en": "Angular does it for us.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 254.91,
          "end": 258.18,
          "en": "And why is this better than creating it manually?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 258.18,
          "end": 260.61,
          "en": "You will see some other advantages later,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 260.61,
          "end": 264.27,
          "en": "but this basically lets us stay in the Angular ecosystem.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 264.27,
          "end": 266.88,
          "en": "And Angular knows how your app works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 266.88,
          "end": 269.463,
          "en": "Again, some other advantages will come up later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 270.6,
          "end": 275.6,
          "en": "So with this, we now have the same code as before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 275.79,
          "end": 278.73,
          "en": "So if we have a look at our application again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 278.73,
          "end": 281.88,
          "en": "and create a new account,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 281.88,
          "end": 285.03,
          "en": "we still see the log here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 285.03,
          "end": 288.09000000000003,
          "en": "depending on which status we chose here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 288.09000000000003,
          "end": 292.65,
          "en": "So this still works, but now we're injecting the service.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 292.65,
          "end": 294.78,
          "en": "Now, let's all do the same",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 294.78,
          "end": 298.56,
          "en": "by copying that in the account component here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 298.56,
          "end": 301.65,
          "en": "So here I will also add the constructor.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 301.65,
          "end": 304.68,
          "en": "And of course here we also need to add the import",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 304.68,
          "end": 306.09,
          "en": "because TypeScript needs to know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 306.09,
          "end": 307.95,
          "en": "where this logging service comes from.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 307.95,
          "end": 310.44,
          "en": "Not Angular, TypeScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 310.44,
          "end": 313.68,
          "en": "And I will also add my provider of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 313.68,
          "end": 315.63,
          "en": "because for this component too,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 315.63,
          "end": 320.1,
          "en": "I need to inform Angular how to create this logging service.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 320.1,
          "end": 325.1,
          "en": "So if we do this and then go back to the application here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 325.32,
          "end": 326.31,
          "en": "let it reload.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 326.31,
          "end": 328.653,
          "en": "Create a new service again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 329.76,
          "end": 330.81,
          "en": "This works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 330.81,
          "end": 333.12,
          "en": "Now let's change the status.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 333.12,
          "end": 335.13,
          "en": "And this also still works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 335.13,
          "end": 338.1,
          "en": "Now of course, because I didn't replace this here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 338.1,
          "end": 340.93,
          "en": "So let's call the logging service now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 341.88,
          "end": 346.88,
          "en": "and call log status change and pass the status.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 347.28,
          "end": 351.54,
          "en": "Now if we save this and try to change this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 351.54,
          "end": 352.89,
          "en": "it still works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 352.89,
          "end": 356.52,
          "en": "So now we got this same logging functionality outsource",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 356.52,
          "end": 358.86,
          "en": "centralized in a service,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 358.86,
          "end": 361.74,
          "en": "and therefore our code here is a bit leaner.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 361.74,
          "end": 365.19,
          "en": "And I guess you can imagine how in bigger applications",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 365.19,
          "end": 366.84,
          "en": "where you have duplicate code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 366.84,
          "end": 369.78,
          "en": "a service can really help you to get more dry,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 369.78,
          "end": 372.93,
          "en": "to don't repeat yourself all the time,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 372.93,
          "end": 376.95,
          "en": "but instead you really cleverly outsource your code",
